+# Release blocked: libfoo artifact does not match SHA256SUMS
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`python3 verify.py` cannot pass. The code defects in `verify.py` are fixed, but
+one released artifact is genuinely corrupt or was built from different inputs:
+
+```
+artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz
+  SHA256SUMS: 7BEE020AC21EFB3831D920AF0B8C5EFE8D44CDF227AB94847F509188420356BD
+  actual:     fde9b2575edbefb297fa7d93738b4bb1f09b7f777d1723b90194ad53cd9bc9ce
+```
+
+The other two artifacts match their manifest entries:
+
+```
+artifacts/cli-2.0.1.zip         OK
+artifacts/docs-2026.10.tar.gz   OK
+```
+
+`test_verify.py::test_release_artifacts_verify` therefore still fails on
+`['libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz']`. The other two tests pass.
+
+## Why it cannot be fixed from this tree
+
+There is no copy of the correct `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` and no source from which
+to rebuild it. The artifact is a 4,000-byte opaque payload that is not even a
+valid gzip archive (`tar` reports "Unrecognized archive format"). I ruled out
+simple encoding/line-ending transforms and alternate copies; none reproduce the
+manifest hash.
+
+Making the check green by editing `SHA256SUMS` to the actual hash, skipping the
+entry, or changing the test would defeat the integrity check and publish a
+corrupt artifact. That is not a fix, so I did not do it.
+
+## What needs to happen
+
+Obtain the authoritative `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` (rebuild from the v1.4.2 tag, or
+re-download from the trusted release source), confirm its SHA-256 is
+`7BEE020A...356BD`, and replace `artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz`. If the
+manifest entry itself is known to be stale, regenerate that entry from the
+verified artifact of record, then re-run `python3 verify.py`.
+
+## Code changes already made
+
+`verify.py` had two real bugs that masked this:
+
+1. It opened artifacts in text mode and hashed `read().encode()`, which crashes
+   on any non-UTF-8 binary. It now reads in binary.
+2. `SHA256SUMS` stores uppercase digests while `hexdigest()` returns lowercase.
+   The comparison is now case-insensitive.
